{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35227","model_call":65,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3443"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q3443"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_5134399#3_8165976","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3443","rank":3,"snippet":"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_5134399#3_8165976\" , \"end_char\": 4074.000000 , \"headings\": \" \" , \"segment\": \"African slaves contributed greatly to the economic and cultural development of the Americas. Their greatest contribution was their labor. Africans brought their expertise, especially in agriculture. They also brought their culture. Their art, music, religion, and food continue to influence American societies. Why did many African rulers participate in the Atlantic slave trade? Lured by profits <cover>African rulers delivered slaves to the Europeans in exchange for gold, guns, and other goods. </cover>THIS SET IS OFTEN IN FOLDERS WITH... Chapter 20 - The Atlantic World - Section 1 - Spai… 12 terms grumhausj Chapter 20 - The Atlantic World - Section 2 - Euro… 12 terms rmal Chapter 20.4 - The Atlantic World - Section 4 - Th… 8 terms grumhausj Chapter 20 - The Atlantic World - Section 2 - Euro… 13 terms grumhausj YOU MIGHT ALSO LIKE... Chapter 20.3 - The Atlantic World - Section 3 - Th… 13 terms ballen60 Chapter 4 section 3 honors world history: The Atla… 18 terms cstechow01 World History Chapter 20 Section 3 18 terms Destiny667 Atlantic Slave trade 11 ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_5134399#3_8165976","rank":3,"relevance":2}]},"time":8},"model_calls":65,"document_judgments":43,"relevance_3":29,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
